That becomes much stronger as a dual-perspective brand universe, not a flat hero-versus-villain campaign.

Wild HAWG is the Beverage Goblin’s natural enemy for one perfect commercial reason: Wild HAWG steals the energy occasion from beverages. The Goblin can hoard every bottle and can—but he cannot capture a pocketable chew.

Wild HAWG	Beverage Goblin
Rewilded boar/outlaw hero	Mischievous collector/trickster
Breaks dependence on cans	Wants every drinking occasion
Freedom, readiness, control	Novelty, temptation, appetite
Matte, metallic, gold/Kintsugi	Dark emerald, neon, brass
“No Can. No Limits.”	“Every drink belongs in the stash.”

The Goblin should not be irredeemably evil, because he has his own brand. He is the villain in HAWG’s telling and the misunderstood protagonist in his own. That gives you two advertisements from every scene.

